From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: enable IPQ5332 REO queue lookup

The IPQ5332 register map lacks two REO LUT control registers,
and the driver disables LUT support despite the vendor hardware
implementation using the same REO LUT protocol as QCN6432.

Restore the two register definitions together with the capability.
This makes the hybrid MLO chips use the same queue lookup protocol.

Reference: Qualcomm TIP wlan-ap 9ac0a9822c6abaf7b0e93746a895b7d5489d189d,
wifi7/hal_qcn9274.c and wifi7/hw.c. Experimental hardware validation
is still required for the exact WBE1.4 firmware family.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -708,7 +708,7 @@
 		.download_calib = true,
 		.supports_suspend = false,
 		.tcl_ring_retry = true,
-		.reoq_lut_support = false,
+		.reoq_lut_support = true,
 		.supports_shadow_regs = false,
 
 		.num_tcl_banks = 48,
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hal_qcn9274.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hal_qcn9274.c
@@ -422,6 +422,8 @@
 	.reo1_sw_cookie_cfg1 = 0x00000070,
 	.reo1_qdesc_lut_base0 = 0x00000074,
 	.reo1_qdesc_lut_base1 = 0x00000078,
+	.reo1_qdesc_addr = 0x0000007c,
+	.reo1_qdesc_max_peerid = 0x00000088,
 	.reo1_ring_base_lsb = 0x00000500,
 	.reo1_ring_base_msb = 0x00000504,
 	.reo1_ring_id = 0x00000508,
